## Step 3: all seven RenderMan quadric primitives in one scene -- Sphere,
## Cone, Cylinder, Hyperboloid, Paraboloid, Torus, Disk. Exercises each
## primitive's own getLocation/getNormal parameterization end to end
## (tessellation, shading, silhouette), not only the isolated
## finite-difference proof tests/normals_test.cpp already covers.
##
## Explicit Clipping: Disk is a flat, camera-facing plate -- the shape that
## hits the near-clip precision defect hardest at the RI_EPSILON default
## (AGENTS.md, "Explicit Clipping where geometry is flat or narrow in z").
## One Clipping for the whole scene since every primitive sits in the same
## z range.
Display "quadrics.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 1400 260 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [65]
Clipping 1 40
Translate 0 0 16
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.2]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.2] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [10 5 0] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 1
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.9]

AttributeBegin
	Translate -9 0 0
	Sphere 1 -1 1 360
AttributeEnd

## Cone, Cylinder, Hyperboloid and Paraboloid all extend along their own
## local z axis by construction (see getLocation in gmanprimitives.cpp);
## rotated here so the shared camera -- looking straight down world z --
## sees each one in profile instead of end-on through its open aperture,
## which would show only a thin silhouette ring, not the characteristic
## shape.
##
## GMAN composes a local transform ahead of everything already accumulated
## (CTM_new = Local . CTM_old under the row-vector convention: a locally
## declared transform applies to the point first, then whatever the CTM
## already carried). Declaring this primitive's own x-offset before its
## "Rotate" therefore rotates the point about the world origin and then
## places it at (x, 0, 0); the pre-WorldBegin "Translate 0 0 16" above
## carries that to camera space afterward, same as every other primitive
## in this scene -- no cancel-and-restore needed.
AttributeBegin
	Translate -6 0 0
	Rotate 90 0 1 0
	Cone 1.5 1 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate -3 0 0
	Rotate 90 0 1 0
	Cylinder 1 -1 1 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Rotate 90 0 1 0
	Hyperboloid 0.3 0 -1  0.9 0 1  360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 3 0 0
	Rotate 90 0 1 0
	Paraboloid 1 0 1.5 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 6 0 0
	Torus 0.8 0.3 -180 180 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 9 0 0
	Disk 0 1 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
